1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
ACT 1 — THE DRONE SEES: head-on intruder; det_v2 detector on a live camera

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Green box = detection; TRACK = perception admission (14.7 fps)

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:32,100
A 20-neuron liquid network flies the approach and the 6-10 m orbit

4
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:39,100
ACT 2 — THE DRONE SEARCHES: target starts BEHIND (azimuth 180°) — empty camera

5
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:46,100
Step-scan with the whole airframe: 40° steps, perimeter sweep

6
00:00:46,100 --> 00:01:06,200
Find, pursue, orbit — all from one 640x480 mono camera

7
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:12,200
ACT 3 — THE DRONE SURVIVES: nominal orbit; perception EMULATED in this act

8
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:18,200
We inject a GPS failure (EKF2_GPS_CTRL=0) — position starts drifting

9
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:30,100
The shield: REFUSE(POS) in ~0.1 s, then a safe D5 descent to touchdown

10
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:37,100
ACT 4 — THE DRONE SPOTS A DECOY: the object circles, never attacks

11
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:45,100
Motion signature: fast, not closing, never below 5 m

12
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:59,700
Label DECOY once the rule holds — the clock is shown openly

13
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:06,700
ACT 4b — THE FLAG REVERSES: the target starts out like a decoy

14
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:15,700
The classifier raises a tentative flag... but the target CHANGES behaviour

15
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:33,800
Descent below 5 m => the label is REVOKED and the drone pursues

16
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:42,800
LiquidPatrol — PX4/Gazebo SITL. Zero zone breaches and zero false refusals across ~140 boots. Controller: a 20-neuron liquid network — 48/48 vs GRU 29/48 on the same grid. Decoys: recognised by behaviour — zero false alarms in the measurements. Home hardware, evenings and weekends.
